    <string name="p_pw_hint">Longer = stronger field and more depth on large objects, but more current and heat.</string>
    <string name="p_d1">Early sample delay (d1)</string>
    <string name="p_d1_hint">Short delay = more sensitive to small and thin objects, but more noise and ground effect.</string>
    <string name="p_d2">Late sample delay (d2)</string>
    <string name="p_d2_hint">The late sample mainly sees large/highly conductive objects; at least 10 µs after d1.</string>
    <string name="p_f">Pulse frequency (f)</string>
    <string name="p_f_hint">Higher = faster response and more averaging, but higher consumption.</string>
    <string name="p_avg">Averaging (avg)</string>
    <string name="p_avg_hint">Pulses per reading: more = smoother signal but slower.</string>
    <string name="p_vcal">Battery calibration (vcal)</string>
